  taste pretty sweet  they're relatively low sugar and i  actually use them to make  toddler friendly pop-tarts which i'll  leave a recipe to  below so definitely check that out now i  don't know what brand of cheese string  that is  but one string cheese typically does  offer about six to seven grams of  protein which  isn't bad for a snack plus it has a  little bit of satiating fat  mozzarella cheese is typically the  lowest sodium cheese  and honestly even though these packaged  snacks  seem super processed fresh mozzarella is  just slightly lower in sodium so if  something like a string cheese is  convenient and easy for you  great i love all cheese but for other  even higher protein options  you could also dip the cherries and  crackers into some greek yogurt or cause  cheese  or make a chia pudding with yogurt and  milk and like  layer the cherries and crush some graham  crackers  on top or inside ah that would legit  taste like cheesecake  and i'm stealing that idea of mine for  myself  so let's take a look at snack b  so this is a bowl of greek yogurt bark  it's basically with greek yogurt  berries and lily's chocolate chips and  this fan has type 1 diabetes and lily's  chocolate chips  are sweet with stevia so they may be a  good choice for people who are watching  their blood sugars  and it looks amazing i mean we've got  protein from the yogurt  carbs and some fiber from the berries  plus little fat  and deliciousness from the chocolate i  mean it's such  a genius snack for summer and one that i  hope people will definitely get some  inspiration from because  i feel like the sky is just the limit on  what you could add here  so i would probably throw in some like  chopped nuts seeds  or hemp parts of course or swirl in some  nut butter for some extra healthy fats  i would also recommend using fuller fat  yogurt i don't know what she's used here  but  we do know and we do have research  linking the consumption of higher fat  dairy  especially fermented dairy like yogurt  to better weight management and better  blood sugar management  and if you have a mild sensitivity to  lactose  going full fat with your dairy may  actually help  because it is lower in lactose and early  research does suggest that one of the  fats in dairy butyric acid  may have some gut protective benefits  it's also just more inherently  saturating and arguably tastes  way better so do not be afraid to go  full fat finally let's take a look at  snack  c  so this is two chia rice cakes topped  with some almond butter and strawberries  looks delish i don't know what brand of  rice cakes this is  but i will say that even the ones that  i'm aware of that have chia in them  are still really low in fat fiber and  protein  i mean we're looking at less than a gram  each it's certainly not a bad option but  i kind of think of  all rice cakes as being pretty low in  nutrition on their own  and are more of like a vehicle for  getting nutrition  in so if the chia ones are way more  expensive than the regular ones  i would probably just go with the cheap  and cheerful bargain ones but i do  love that we have some fiber protein and  healthy fats in the nut butter  and some carbs in the strawberries and  rice cakes  but i would say if you did want the  benefits of chia i would probably just  sprinkle a little bit of the chia on top  or flax or hemp hearts or any other  nutrient-dense sprinkle  that you like but delicious combo and  totally something that i would do  myself so whoa we have a lot of amazing  ideas here and  i would be totally thrilled with any or  all of them  i mean can somebody please come over and  make me a meal  soon and if i didn't cover yours like i  said  i'm choosing randomly so check out the  description box for how to submit your  meals today  and of course a reminder to please be  kind and supportive in the comments  and if you like this video be sure to  give it the thumbs up  let me know that you like this if you  want more videos like this  leave me a comment below on your  thoughts on this new series concept did  you like it did you get something out of  it was it fun  i want to know also subscribe to the  channel and i will see you next time on  abby's kitchen  bye  you
 

